==Translingual==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[']]
* {{sense|transliterated Cyrillic}} [[′]]

===Symbol===
'''’'''
# An [[apostrophe]].
## Indicating a possessive, with ''s'', in English.
## Indicating the omission of letters, in English.
# A [[closing]] [[quotation mark]].
# {{context| in [[transliterate]]d [[Cyrillic]] text}} Transliteration of the [[soft sign]] ([[ь]]), indicating [[palatalization]] of preceding consonants.
# {{context| in [[transliterate]]d [[Arabic]] and [[Hebrew]] text}} Transliteration of the [[glottal stop]] ([[hamza]]).
# A [[glottal stop]] in the orthography of numerous languages of America, Africa, and formally the Pacific. In most [[Polynesian]] languages, the convention has shifted to the [[okina]] <[[ʻ]]>.
# {{informal}} A substitute for the combining diacritic [[ʼ]] used in the [[International Phonetic Alphabet]] for [[ejective]] and other glottalized consonants.

